body:
![high](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/high-priority.svg)

There is a potential memory leak if the component unmounts while `fetchMsSourceRevealAsset` is in flight. If unmounting occurs before the promise resolves, the cleanup function runs first (setting `isMountedRef.current = false` and revoking any existing object URL). When the promise subsequently resolves, `URL.createObjectURL` is called and assigned to `msSourceRevealUrlRef.current` after unmount, meaning it will never be revoked. To prevent this, check `isMountedRef.current` immediately after the fetch resolves and before creating the object URL.

```javascript
      try {
        const asset = await fetchMsSourceRevealAsset(routeRequest);
        if (!isMountedRef.current) {
          return;
        }
        const nextUrl = URL?.createObjectURL ? URL.createObjectURL(asset.blob) : null;
        if (msSourceRevealUrlRef.current && URL?.revokeObjectURL) {
          URL.revokeObjectURL(msSourceRevealUrlRef.current);
        }
        msSourceRevealUrlRef.current = nextUrl;

        setMsSourceRevealState({
          status: 'ready',
          assetUrl: nextUrl,
          error: null,
        });
      }
